{
  "body": [
    {
      "anchor": "h:about-readmes",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "About READMEs",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "{% data reusables.repositories.about-READMEs %}",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "For more information about providing guidelines for your project, see ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "AUTOTITLE",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ],
          "internal": true,
          "target": "/communities/setting-up-your-project-for-healthy-contributions/adding-a-code-of-conduct-to-your-project",
          "type": "link"
        },
        {
          "text": " and ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "AUTOTITLE",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ],
          "internal": true,
          "target": "/communities/setting-up-your-project-for-healthy-contributions",
          "type": "link"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "A README is often the first item a visitor will see when visiting your repository. README files typically include information on:",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "text": "What the project does",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "text": "Why the project is useful",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "text": "How users can get started with the project",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "text": "Where users can get help with your project",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "text": "Who maintains and contributes to the project",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "ordered": false,
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "If you put your README file in your repository's hidden ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": ".github",
          "type": "code"
        },
        {
          "text": ", root, or ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "docs",
          "type": "code"
        },
        {
          "text": " directory, {% data variables.product.github %} will recognize and automatically surface your README to repository visitors.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "If a repository contains more than one README file, then the file shown is chosen from locations in the following order: the ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": ".github",
          "type": "code"
        },
        {
          "text": " directory, then the repository's root directory, and finally the ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "docs",
          "type": "code"
        },
        {
          "text": " directory.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "When your README is viewed on GitHub, any content beyond 500 KiB will be truncated.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "{% data reusables.profile.profile-readme %}",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "h:auto-generated-table-of-contents-for-markdown-files",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "Auto-generated table of contents for markdown files",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "For the rendered view of any Markdown file in a repository, including README files, {% data variables.product.github %} will automatically generate a table of contents based on section headings. You can view the table of contents for a README file by clicking the \"Outline\" menu icon {% octicon \"list-unordered\" aria-label=\"Table of Contents\" %} in the top corner of the rendered page.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "h:section-links-in-markdown-files-and-blob-pages",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "text": "Section links in markdown files and blob pages",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "level": 2,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    "<8 more items>"
  ],
